{{Quote|I gotta get one of those...|Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 3: The Sin">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref>}}
'''Jetpacks''', also known as '''jump packs''', '''rocket-packs''', and '''thruster packs''', were personal aerial transportation devices that allowed the operator to fly into and through the air with great mobility. [[Mandalorian armor]] was equipped with jetpacks, and was used by some [[clone trooper]]s in the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]].

Multiple military forces employed [[soldier]]s equipped with jetpacks, with trooper variants including the [[clone jetpack trooper]], the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[jumptrooper]], the [[First Order jet trooper]], and the [[Sith Eternal]]'s [[Sith Jetpack Trooper]].

Jetpack models included the [[JT-12 jetpack]], the [[Z-6 jetpack]], and [[rocket pack]]s.

==Characteristics==
{{Quote|When you have healed, you will begin your drills. Until you know it, it will not listen to your commands.|"[[The Armorer]]" tells Din Djarin of using a jetpack|<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>}}
[[File:TheMandosJetpack-SWL98.png|thumb|left|250px|A jetpack enabled its wearer to fly.]]
Jetpacks were usually worn on the back and controlled by a wrist-mounted device. Due to that, a jetpack could technically be operated by the user when not wearing it.<ref name="Chapter 10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref> Training was required to master the use of a jetpack, with inexperienced flyers being unable to control the device properly.<ref name="Chapter 8" /> Jetpacks could be used in "rocket mode," propelling them at great speeds, thereby making them a harder target for anti-aircraft systems.<ref name="Imperial Troops">{{EncyclopediaCite|Imperial Troops}}</ref>

The Z-6 jetpack featured a missile that could launch from the top of the jetpack.<ref name="The Mandalore Plot">{{TCW|The Mandalore Plot}}</ref> A variant was used by the various [[clone trooper]] units of the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Grand Army of the Republic|Grand Army]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="TCW film">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref>

==History==
[[File:Jetpack-TSWB.png|thumb|right|250px|A Mandalorian jetpack of the [[Heavy Infantry Mandalorian]]-class]]
Bounty hunters such as [[Jango Fett]]<ref name="AoR-JF1">[[Age of Republic - Jango Fett 1|''Age of Republic - Jango Fett'' 1]]</ref>, and later his son, [[Boba Fett|Boba]], used jetpacks in their various jobs.<ref name="Ep. IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> [[Mandalorian]] tradition identified the jetpack as the art of the [[Rising Phoenix]].<ref name="Chapter 8" /> Mandalorian factions such as [[Death Watch]] used jetpacks against their enemies.<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> The Republic's Grand Army's clone troopers would use jetpacks to assist them in their missions.<ref name="TCW film" /> During the [[Siege of Mandalore]], clone troopers and [[Mandalorian warrior]]s fought side-by-side, with former [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] returning to the [[Republic Military]] as an [[advisor]] for the campaign. While [[Clone Commander]] [[Rex]] forgot to pack her a jetpack, Tano improvised by jumping from their [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] [[gunship]], fighting and jumping from [[Starship|ship]] to ship until reaching the Mandalorian [[capital]] of [[Sundari]].<ref name="Old Friends">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref>

[[File:Jumptrooper2-TITSWE.png|thumb|left|250px|An Imperial Jumptrooper]]
The [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[jumptrooper]]s used jetpacks to enforce Imperial rule, which led to their deployment into conflicts like the [[Galactic Civil War]]<ref name="BF2">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> and the [[Mandalorian Civil War (Imperial Era)|Mandalorian Civil War]], in which jetpack-equipped stormtroopers fought jetpack-using Mandalorian rebels.<ref name="Heroes of Mandalore">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Heroes of Mandalore]]''</ref> The [[First Order]] later deployed similar [[First Order jet trooper|jet troopers]] in its own campaign for galactic conquest. Both the Empire's and First Order's rivals, the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and [[Resistance]], respectively, also employed jetpack troopers. Beyond both sides making use of a class of soldier known as a [[rocket-jumper]],<ref name="BF2" /> the [[Alliance Army]] made use of a class of [[Jetpack Trooper]]s.<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> The [[Sith Eternal army]] maintained a force of [[Sith Jetpack Trooper]]s.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

